[Music]  hi everyone i'm anushari bostava and  today we're going to be talking about  vertex ai's automl by google cloud as a  recap automl is a no code solution that  allows us to create high quality custom  models with minimal effort and ml  expertise with automl you can train a  model for different data types such as  image text tabular or even video data  today we're going to look at a concrete  example with natural language  understanding for text data  automl natural language allows you to  perform supervised learning which  involves training a computer to  recognize patterns from labeled data  using supervised learning you can train  a custom model to recognize content that  you care about and text  the use cases for this flavor of  automela include entity extraction  sentiment analysis and text  classification  what sort of problems can you solve with  these options  entity extraction allows you to create a  model that expects a document for known  entities reference in the document and  then label those entities in the text so  you can use this for example to extract  key players such as people company  locations in a structured manner from  news articles  a good use for sentiment analysis is  when you want to identify the prevailing  emotional opinion within text  specifically determine a writer's  attitude as positive negative or neutral  and last but not least text  classification and that is what we are  going to do today  let's say i'm working at a company and  we just launched a new version of our  app we're starting to scale up and we  really want to meet our customers needs  we are thrilled that our app is growing  explosively but it's getting harder to  properly route our incoming user reports  and we spend a lot of time triaging what  are either bug reports billing issues or  feedback you could use a pre-trained api  for nlp  however the general model does not  understand the specific nuances we need  in this scenario  if your text consists of news articles  or other content you want to categorize  or if you want to discover the sentiment  of your examples the pre-trained natural  language api is worth trying  but if your text examples don't fit  neatly into sentiment based or the  vertical topic based classification  scheme available in the natural language  api and you want to use your own labels  instead it's worth experimenting with a  custom classifier to see if it fits your  needs  just like in our use case  so let's go into vertex ai and see  exactly how we build this model we can  then integrate into our feedback system  here we are in the vertex ai console we  have our data set already with the  feedback we've already collected and  most importantly labeled then we go into  the trainings tab select a couple  options automl will split the data for  me between training test and validation  and it's off to the races  the default for training  is 80 of your data but you can manually  adjust the division if needed  the vast majority of your data should be  in the training set this is the data  your model sees during training it's  used to learn the parameters of the  model namely the weights of the  connections between the nodes in the  neural network  the validation set sometimes also called  the dev set is also used during the  training process  after the model learning framework  incorporates the training data during  each iteration of the training process  it uses the model's performance on the  validation set to tune the model  the test set is not involved during the  training process  after the model has completed its  training automl natural language uses  the test set as a challenge for your  model  the performance of your model on the  test set is intended to give you an idea  of how your model will perform on  real-world data  once the model is done training we can  check out our model here in the models  tab we click on the model name and there  are a few mechanisms for us to evaluate  the model such as the precision and  recall the confusion matrix which shows  how often the model classified each  label correctly shows in blue  the test and deploy tab allows us to  deploy our model to a rest endpoint so  we can then easily call it from a web or  mobile app  it also lets us make sample predictions  here from within the ui  let's try out a sample  the loading times are so slow now on my  pixel 4.  the model correctly identified this as a  bug report  let's do one more just for fun  thank you for this release the new  features are great  we can see the model predicted this as  general feedback with a high confidence  score  now let's say we want to use this model  from a phone or web app so right here in  vertex ai we can see the python code we  would need to call this cloud hosted  model from our apps  client libraries and other languages are  available too  i can repeat what we just did in the  console making predictions  programmatically in my code and then  make decisions in my app based on the  model's output  so there you go now you can see how as  developers we can easily build machine  learning models to solve our problems  and directly integrate them into our  apps and services all without a phd  check out the guide on getting started  with automl natural language processing  and let us know what you think  [Music]

